plans.f2a7af1b6bcf133506389c2d8b1caa7d:
{"text":"There is a direct conflict on this. Two Sales rules disagree on whether store credit counts in Norway orders. One says Norway orders include orders paid with store credit and gift cards, converted to euros at the daily rate, last checked 5 September 2026 [itm_giftstorecredit]. The other says Norway orders count only card and cash payments, with store credit and gift cards left out, last checked 2 October 2026 [itm_giftcardonly]. The owner of Sales marked these two as disagreeing, and I can't say which one is right. The Sales owners are Jon Abara and Sofia Brandt, and that decision is theirs.

There is also a relevant event: online sales to Norway stopped on 4 August 2026 under a new customs rule, so Norway orders fell to almost nothing after that date, last checked 3 October 2026 [itm_norwaystop]. Its note says fewer orders in Norway after 4 August do not mean fewer customers.

The Orders metric is defined as the value of completed and paid orders in euros at the daily rate, with cancelled orders and failed payments left out, from Cube [metric:orders].","calls":[]}

